add(1613,'quant-distribution','Quantization does not imply Gaussian noise','What is missing from the claimed mapping “encoder ±0.088° → Gaussian noise σ=0.001 rad”?',[
('A justified error distribution and interpretation of the bound/resolution; the bound alone does not determine Gaussianity or sigma.','Unit conversion alone is insufficient.'),('Only a new name for the degree unit; every bounded error is exactly Gaussian.','A finite bound does not imply an unbounded Gaussian distribution.'),('Only the policy’s GPU core count, because that uniquely determines encoder noise.','Compute resources do not determine the encoder error law.'),('Nothing; ±0.088° is exactly equal to σ=0.001 rad by unit conversion.','The converted half-width is about 0.001536 rad, and half-width is not automatically sigma.')],'A Gaussian approximation can be a modeling choice, but it must be declared rather than inferred from the displayed bound.',kind='table',conflict='The observation-noise row presents a quantization-bound-to-Gaussian-sigma implication without a distribution or convention.',locator='Observation noise row and encoder example.')
